{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127522-coteries-at-higher-levels","id":1127522,"title":"Coteries at Higher Levels?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-11T01:49:51-07:00","id":1127522,"title":"Coteries at Higher Levels?","content":"<b>How do you run them?</b><br /> <br /> It's easy to do when your characters are all yung'uns who, in the words of Jack, are <i>&quot;bossed around by every vampire with a week of seniority over you.&quot; </i>but as vampires grow in age and power, they don't seem to want to do things by themselves and instead manipulate the lesser vampires into doing their work for them.<br /> <br /> So how exactly does a coterie of Ancillae,Elder, or even Ancient vampires work? If you've got a story hook that requires a group of 3-5 millennia old vampires to resolve, that probably means the end of the world is happening, or some crazy shit like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T02:02:49-07:00","id":1127524,"title":"","content":"Elder-level Vampire started to make more sense to me when I realized that the fantasy is simultaneously being 700 years old and also hanging around goth clubs and fighting werewolves in back alleys. You don't need to change the world, you can just hang out with your immortal badass friends and fight other immortal badasses whom you probably spilled wine on at Versailles. That's a fun thing to sit around the gaming table and roll dice for.<br /> <br /> Elders live in the present, not the past. If I were running a game for a coterie of old farts, my default pitch would probably be like &quot;It's been 50 years since the four of you have been in the same room together. Remember that Dragon you all hate for killing your friend in 1870? She's the Prince of Cleveland now, and you just got to Cleveland. What are you gonna do about that, and what are each of you doing after the meeting tonight?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:05:18-07:00","id":1127640,"title":"","content":"The easiest way is if being in the coteries is how they go that higher level. They might not work together as much, but they'll have proven themselves to one another - rightly or wrongly, honestly or deceptively - in a way that few other vampires would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:58:18-07:00","id":1128024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1127522-coteries-at-higher-levels#post1127522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How do you run them?</b><br /> <br /> It's easy to do when your characters are all yung'uns who, in the words of Jack, are <i>&quot;bossed around by every vampire with a week of seniority over you.&quot; </i>but as vampires grow in age and power, they don't seem to want to do things by themselves and instead manipulate the lesser vampires into doing their work for them.<br /> <br /> So how exactly does a coterie of Ancillae,Elder, or even Ancient vampires work? If you've got a story hook that requires a group of 3-5 millennia old vampires to resolve, that probably means the end of the world is happening, or some crazy shit like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Thousand years of night could be a thing for you.","